{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310840,"nonce":"qz7hhjeQohbe4iVTDXMZXUgf74g=","title":"Phase (c) investigation snapshot. Llama 3.2 1B Q4_K_M runs end-to-end on Rayzor today (~2 GB resident, ~3 s/token), but produces incoherent ...","message":"- Loading: Q6_K embed + Q4_K attention/FFN, 16 layers, 2.1 GB resident at 4K ctx cap. F32 norms load with correct values (output_norm gain = 2.45, etc).\n- Forward pass executes: 16 blocks complete, no NaNs propagating, intermediate values in plausible ranges.\n- LM head dot product produces logits in `[-8.5, 8.0]` with `mean|v| = 1.83` and a clear argmax. Healthy enough to not be pure noise.\n- RoPE base = 500000 (correct for Llama 3); LUT spot-check `cos[0,0]=1`, `cos[1,0]=0.5403`, `sin[1,0]=0.8415` matches `cos(1 rad)`, `sin(1 rad)`. RoPE init is correct.\n- Tokenizer encodes prompt correctly: `[791, 6864, 315, 9822, 374]` for `\"The capital of France is\"` (matches HF tokenization).\n- KV cache pre-allocated at 4096 tokens, F32. Per-layer 268 MB total; would benefit from F16 (next halving) and from a 1K-2K default cap.\n\n\n- For `\"The capital of France is\"` argmax → `91 ('|')`. Expected `Paris` (token 12366 ish). Logit gap between top tokens is small (max 8.0, mean abs 1.8 → top ~4x mean) suggesting the model is *under-confident*, not just *wrong*. \n- Output `\"The capital of France is|� ofTags� }�� balance\"` — the `�` glyphs are byte-fallback tokens decoded as raw bytes by the tokenizer's `decode`. Not a bug per se, but suggests the model is sampling tokens that don't form valid UTF-8 sequences together.\n\n\n1. **Attention mask shift wrong during prefill** — `applyMask(scores, positionOffset)` with `positionOffset = cache.currentLen` (= 0 on prefill). The mask diagonal needs to shift by `positionOffset` so query row `i` can attend to keys `[0, i + positionOffset]`. Worth re-deriving from llama.cpp's reference to confirm sign / off-by-one.\n\n2. **GQA expansion direction** — Q heads share KV heads (32 Q over 8 KV → 4 Q per KV group). The `expandKvHeads` step at `GQAttention.hx:103` broadcasts each KV head G=4 times. If the repeat axis is wrong, head-i's Q would attend to a wrong-head KV pair.\n\n3. **Q6_K dequant subtle precision** — `bugs_gguf_q6k_and_f32_load` confirms the block decode matches the Python reference *exactly* for a single block. But the embed table has 128256 × 8 = 1.03M blocks; a cumulative drift wouldn't show on the per-block unit test. Sanity check: compute MSE of our dequant'd embed vs a reference Python dequant for the same GGUF, expect \u003c 1e-7 RMS.\n\n4. **Embedding direction (Llama embeds are oriented row=vocab, col=hidden)** — `Embedding.lookup(tokenIds)` does `weight.gatherRows(tokenIds)` which expects `weight: [vocab, hidden]`. The `decodeQ6KRaw` produces a QTensor with `rows=info.dims[last]=vocab=128256, cols=hidden=2048` via the `PyTorch [out, in]` convention from `bugs_q4_km_layout_and_linear_convention`. Looks right but worth a direct pixel-of-pixel comparison with HF.\n\n5. **Final hidden state magnitude** — `[fwd] outputNorm x[0,0]=0.39` is on the low side; reference Llama typically gives final hidden state RMS ≈ 1.0-2.5 before LM head. If the hidden state is underweighted, logits are uniformly small (which we observe). RMSNorm itself is unit-RMS normalized; the gain (2.45) determines absolute scale.\n\n\n1. **Pixel comparison vs HF**: run `transformers` on the same prompt with the same GGUF (via `gguf-tools` to dequant first), capture the per-layer hidden state at layer 0 / 8 / 15 and the final logits top-10. Compare to Rayzor's. The layer where Rayzor's hidden state first deviates is the bug.\n\n2. **Single-token oracle**: feed prompt `\"Hello\"` (token 9906) and capture the prefill logits. The argmax should be one of `{\",\", \" world\", \" everyone\", \"!\"}` (tokens 11, 1917, 7288, 0). Same for `\"def fibonacci\"` → expect ` (`. These are deterministic-enough to red-flag a broken model.\n\n3. **Attention sanity**: replace `applyMask` with `identity` (no mask) and re-run. If logits change *significantly*, the mask sign is wrong. If they barely change at prefill seq_len=5, the mask shape might be only-self-attending.\n\n\n- ~3 s/token on 5-token generation. Single-threaded matmul (NumaPool not wired per `feedback_numa_pure_haxe`); per-op malloc overhead. Phase B from the original 9-phase plan (arena allocator + NumaPool + fused kernels) is the path to LiteRT-comparable speed. None of that work blocks coherence — coherence is upstream of all of it.\n\n\n- [[bugs-gguf-q6k-and-f32-load]] — the load-time bugs that made the pipeline run at all.\n- [[bugs-array-map-float-audit]] / [[feature-double-and-array-stringifier]] — the f64-precision sweep that fixed Float storage end-to-end. Coherence may still depend on f64 round-trip in places we haven't audited (attention scores arithmetic, softmax intermediates).\n- Original 9-phase plan in session context (compiler/.../plan.md memo) — Phases 1-7 done, 8-9 are the demo. Phase 9 = this file.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_llama_chat_coherence_status` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}